        "'All Pre-fixed Returns are not Riba': the Shari'ah test is the nature of the transaction, not whether the return is fixed — a fixed trade profit margin or fixed Ijarah rent is valid, while any addition on a loan/debt (fixed or not) is Riba.",
        "The analogy 'if predetermined Ijarah rent is allowed, predetermined loan interest should be too' is explicitly refuted: Ijarah rent reflects an asset's inherently uncertain usufruct-generating capacity over its economic life, and only non-consumable assets (not money) can be leased.",
