        "Islamic finance requires two distinct benchmark/reference-rate types (unlike conventional finance's single interest rate): a price (markup/rent) scale for debt/semi-debt contracts, and a sharing-ratio scale for equity contracts.",
        "Using a conventional interest-rate benchmark merely as a pricing reference number for Islamic trade/Ijarah transactions does not itself make the transaction un-Islamic, provided the substantive Shari'ah rules of trade/Ijarah are actually followed."
