    "'Al Kharaj bi-al-Daman' / 'Al Ghunm bil Ghurm' (no gain without bearing loss liability) is the universal Shari'ah test for the legality of any return on capital, applied differently across loans, trade, Ijarah and Shirkah.",
    "'All Pre-fixed Returns are not Riba': the Shari'ah test is the nature of the transaction (sale/lease vs loan/debt), not whether the return is fixed — enabling Islamic banks to use interest-rate benchmarks merely as pricing references without becoming un-Islamic.",
    "Islamic banks 'deal in goods and documents, not money' (unlike conventional banks, which 'deal in documents, not goods') — they must take genuine asset ownership and bear real risk, which is the source of their distinctive additional risks (asset, Shari'ah non-compliance, rate-of-return, legal, withdrawal).",
